For apparent reasons you cannot sacrifice a corpse if you have
_finished_ eating it, but if you're interrupted it's possible; the
weight is apparently reduced and the god accepts your gift. If, OTOH,
the corpse got too old (more than 50 turns) your god won't accept it;
but since the age counter is reset (AFAIK) if you eat the corpse decay
shouldn't be a problem.

It might be possible that amnesia already stroke me, and I might
misremember that fact, but it should be easy for you to try it out in
Wizmode...
Look for an altar level, kill some (heavy) monster, engrave Elbereth,
create some more monsters (to interrupt your meal), try lifting the
(heavy) corpse, start eating, get interrupted, check weight reduction
(may need more than one bite to become light enough), sacrifice.

